{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:18.55.260","page_type":"section"},"citation":"18.55.260","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.55.260","content_hash":"7d3e23159c891aac9ee7bb109d84d0e9058b280c304f82d47d0723bdabcf1865","heading":"“Z” definitions.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:18.55.260:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.55.260","text":"“Zone” means an area within which certain uses of land and buildings are permitted and certain others are prohibited, yards and other open spaces are required, lot areas, building height limits, and other requirements are established, all of the foregoing being identical for the zone in which they apply.\n“Zoning district” means a specifically delineated area or section of the City of Topeka shown on the zoning map within which regulations and requirements uniformly govern the use, placement, spacing and size of land and buildings.\n“Zoning lot” means a parcel of land under single ownership that is of sufficient size to meet minimum zoning requirements for area, coverage, and use, and that can provide such yards and other open spaces as required by this division.\n“Zoning map” means the official map or maps which are a part of the zoning ordinance and delineate the boundaries of the zoning districts.\n“Zoning regulations” means the lawfully adopted zoning map and zoning ordinances of the City of Topeka. (Ord. 19370 § 103, 3-23-10. Code 1995 Appx. C, Art. XXXV.)","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"bd2ea49d-f711-5d4b-9909-7d149bbc8136"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"18.55.260","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/18.55.260","content_hash":"f054c64f9674ae9adbe594025bcc657aa026f09560720d